        "dependencies": ["calc-deriv-003b-h2"],
        "title": "Take the Limit",
        "text": "$f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0}(4x + 2h + 3)$\n\nAs $h \\to 0$:\n\n$f'(x) = 4x + 0 + 3 = 4x + 3$\n\nVerify using the power rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}(2x^2 + 3x) = 4x + 3$",
